decisions.decision:
List only what waits on Inês herself. Leave out:
- declined cards (payment_due);
- students who haven't signed in yet;
- a card not yet added;
- Meet 'needs a one-time setup' (!configured);
- Meet's pending sync count;
- a failed Meet status fetch;
- expression drafts;
- lessons left on a day off;
- a returning student's ordinary new booking.

decisions.why:
Every student cancel path writes both columns: handleCancel (3706), completeRefund via requested_by (3641-3643), handleStopSeries (3127) and retryRefunds. A cancelled lesson silently drops off her week today (TeacherSchedule.tsx:268-270). Design 1's 'Add a lesson here' is dropped for three reasons:
- the slot is open to students the instant it is cancelled;
- it may already be taken;
- opening LessonDetails on a cancelled row would still offer Move and Cancel.

decisions.decision:
Items clear themselves:
- changes and cancellations after 72 elapsed hours, or once the lesson's time has passed;
- first lessons and welcomes outside the 7 days before the lesson, once it starts, or once the welcome is sent;
- Meet and payment items when resolved.
There is no dismiss button.

After 'Send welcome email' finishes, either way:
- on success, show 'Welcome sent to {first name}.' in the existing status strip;
- on failure or a 409, show the Worker's message in the existing error strip;
- reload students and move focus to the week heading.

files.change:
- Type-only imports of AdminStudent, GoogleMeetConnection and PaymentReview.
- Constants NEEDS_YOU_RECENT_HOURS = 72 and NEEDS_YOU_AHEAD_DAYS = 7.
- Type NeedsYouItem, a union:
  - {kind:'meet'; key:'meet'; reconnect:boolean}
  - {kind:'payment'; key; review; part:'lesson'|'fee'|'refund'}
  - {kind:'welcome'; key; student; at}
  - {kind:'changed'; key; booking; count; first:boolean}
  - {kind:'cancelled'; key; booking; count}
  - {kind:'first'; key; booking}
- Pure function needsYou({ now, meet, payments, students, lessons, cancellations }). It applies the rules, grouping and order in userFacing, builds keys from the first booking id of each group, and returns [] when nothing waits.

Next to the lesson-card rules (about 1910-1922), add:
